test-pipe-address.js: upstream names these for the transport rather than the module, but the subject is net.Server and net.Socket over a Unix domain socket
test-pipe-abstract-socket.js: as test-pipe-address.js; a Linux abstract-namespace socket is still net.Server and net.Socket
test-pipe-writev.js: as test-pipe-address.js; exercises net.Socket's vectored write over a pipe transport
test-pipe-stream.js: as test-pipe-address.js; a net.Server over a pipe, piped into and out of
test-pipe-unref.js: as test-pipe-address.js; net.Server.unref over a pipe transport
test-listen-fd-ebadf.js: upstream names it for the fd rather than the module; the subject is net.Server.listen refusing a descriptor that is not a socket
test-destroy-socket-in-lookup.js: upstream names it for the operation rather than the module; the subject is net.Socket.destroy during the DNS lookup that precedes connect
test-gc-net-timeout.js: upstream names it for the collection it forces; the subject is a net.Socket timeout
test-ref-unref-return.js: upstream names it for the operation; the subject is that ref and unref return the socket, on both net and dgram
